  "releaseNotes": "LuciferCore High-Performance LastIndexOf Vectorization Update\n\n      Core Architectural Enhancements\n      - Accelerated Backward Scan: Eradicated legacy backward scalar loops by leveraging net 9 LastIndexOfAny SIMD intrinsics for case-insensitive byte searching.\n      - Low-Level Char-to-Byte Routing: Implemented an aggressive memory-remapping layer via MemoryMarshal for ASCII characters, transforming sluggish char searches into direct hardware-level byte vector operations.\n      - High-Throughput Reverse Sub-Span Matching: Engineered an optimized LastIndexOfSubSpanIgnoreCase routine powered by a backward SIMD Skip mechanism, drastically reducing cache-miss penalties.\n\n      Performance Breakthrough Results\n      - Case-Insensitive Char Scan: Reverse search speeds surged by an incredible 22x, slashing 268MB data array latency from 645ms down to just 29.3ms.\n      - Case-Insensitive Byte Scan: Backward byte lookups execute up to 8.3 times faster, matching raw thô non-normalized memory speeds at 14.9ms for large-scale buffers with absolute Zero Allocation.",
